{"name":"Movie Star","hex":"#c52033","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"movie star","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A leading actor in a movie, especially one perceived as a celebrity."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/movie_star"}],"entries":[{"title":"Movie star","blocks":[{"text":"A movie star is an actor who is famous for their starring, or leading, roles in movies. The term is used for performers who are marketable stars as they become popular household names and whose names are used to promote movies, for example in trailers and posters. The most prominent movie stars are known in the industry as bankable stars."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Movie_star","wikidata":"Q1337738"},{"title":"Film","blocks":[{"text":"A film, movie, or motion picture is a work of visual art that simulates experiences and otherwise communicates ideas, stories, perceptions, emotions, or atmosphere through the use of moving images that are generally, since the 1930s, synchronized with sound and sometimes feature other sensory stimuli."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Le_Voyage_dans_la_Lune_%281902%29.webm/330px--Le_Voyage_dans_la_Lune_%281902%29.webm.jpg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Film","wikidata":"Q11424"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Less_Than_the_Dust_2.jpg/500px-Less_Than_the_Dust_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Less_Than_the_Dust_2.jpg/500px-Less_Than_the_Dust_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Poster advertising a 1916 film with Mary Pickford, one of the first movie stars","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALess_Than_the_Dust_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4a/%D9%83%D8%B1%D9%8A%D9%85_%D8%B9%D8%A8%D8%AF_%D8%A7%D9%84